  "texts": {
    "preamble": "& vs The Union Of India on 12 December, 2024 Author: Anita Sumanth Bench: Anita Sumanth 2024:Mhc:4190 In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated: 12.12.2024 Coram The Honourable Dr. Justice Anita Sumanth And The Honourable Mr.Justice G. Arul Murugan W.A. Nos. 2103, 2105, 2107 & 2109 of 2019 & C.M.P. Nos. 14263, 14264, 14268, 14269, 14271, 14273, 14278 & 14281 2019 Dr. Rajkumar Yeddula ..Appella No. 210 P. Kavusalia .. Appella No.2105 o D. Ramachandran ..Appella No. 2107 A.Kamalavinayagam ..Appella No. 2109 Vs. 1. The Union of India, rep. by its Secretary, Ministry of Health and Family Welfare, 156, 'A' wing, Nirman Bhavan, New Delhi 110 011. 1\\6 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis 2. The Chairperson, Food Safety and Standards Authority of India, FDA Bhavan, Kotla Road, & vs The Union Of India on 12 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/195190022/ 1 New Delhi 110 002. 3. The Chief Executive Officer, The Chairperson, Food Safety and Standards Authority of India, FDA Bhavan, Kotla Road, New Delhi 110 002. 4. The Executive Director, The Chairperson, Food Safety and Standards Authority of India, FDA Bhavan, Kotla Road, New Delhi 110 002. 5. The Director, Food Safety and Standards Authority of India, Southern Regional Office, 2nd Floor, Central Documentation Complex, Ch.P.T. Building, Rajaji Salai, Chennai 600 001. ..Respo the Wri Prayer: Writ Appeals as against the order dated 24.04.20 W.P. No. 11974, 11980, 11959 & 12011 of 2019 respectively. 2\\6 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis For Appellant :: M/s.K. Thennan in all appeals K. Mohanamurali For Respondents in all appeals :: Mr.S. Janarthanam for R Mr.V. Ashok Kumar for Mr.Su. Srinivasan, Standing Counsel for R2 JUDGMENT (Delivered by DR. ANITA SUMANTH,J.) Originally, 14 persons had filed writ petitions challenging recruitment notification dated 26.03.2019 issued by the Food Safety and Standards Authority of India. The writ petitions came to be dismissed by way of impugned order dated 24.04.2019 on the ground that the petitioners are contractual employees and hence, not entitled to challenge the recruitment notification. & vs The Union Of India on 12 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/195190022/ 2 2. All 14 writ petitioners instituted writ appeals that came to be dismissed for non-prosecution.",
    "facts": "As against the termination of the contracts, the appellants state that they have approached the Delhi High Court by way of writ petitions.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
